# --- secrets (kit shipped none of this; add BEFORE first commit) ---
.env
.env.*
# No `!.env.example` negation. It was here from the first commit, and on the first push to
# GitHub the secret scanner refused the push: a **live Groq API key** was sitting in
# `.env.example:16`, committed in S2 and carried through every commit since. The key has been
# rotated and the file is purged from history (S12).
#
# The negation is not coming back. A tracked env template is a file whose whole job is to
# look harmless while sitting one careless paste away from being a credential — and the
# thing it existed to provide now exists somewhere better: `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` lists every
# variable, its default and what breaks without it, and it cannot hold a value by accident
# because it is prose.
#
# Keep a local `.env.example` if you like. It stays on your disk.
*.pem
*.key
.claude/settings.local.json
.mcp.json

